WEBVTT

01:33.510 --> 01:36.390
If there's anything I lack
as a presidential candidate,

01:36.470 --> 01:38.430
please don't hesitate to criticize me.

01:39.020 --> 01:41.940
Thank you for listening.

01:42.520 --> 01:43.560
Okay.

01:43.650 --> 01:45.440
If you can do this in the actual event,

01:45.520 --> 01:46.940
it should be fine.

01:47.020 --> 01:49.400
Yes, I'd have to do this
in the actual event too.

01:49.480 --> 01:50.570
Are you worried?

01:50.650 --> 01:52.110
At the general meeting,

01:52.200 --> 01:53.820
didn't you express yourself clearly?

01:53.910 --> 01:55.030
That's because

01:55.120 --> 01:57.200
I was so focused on facing my own feelings

01:57.280 --> 01:58.490
that it flowed smoothly.

01:58.580 --> 01:59.990
Besides, the audience tomorrow

02:00.080 --> 02:03.080
should be more packed than before, right?

02:03.160 --> 02:04.710
Yes.

02:04.790 --> 02:06.420
Tomorrow, the whole school

02:06.500 --> 02:07.960
will fill this auditorium.

02:09.550 --> 02:11.840
But we're doing the same thing.

02:11.920 --> 02:14.430
You just focus on speaking your mind.

02:14.510 --> 02:16.510
I don't think that will work.

02:17.470 --> 02:20.600
When I saw the way you spoke
at the general meeting,

02:20.680 --> 02:22.180
I understood right away.

02:22.270 --> 02:23.690
What should I do

02:23.770 --> 02:26.270
to be able to talk like you?

02:26.350 --> 02:29.610
Even if you ask me what to do,

02:29.690 --> 02:32.400
it's the only thing
that truly requires experience.

02:35.950 --> 02:38.580
Then let me teach you a secret plan
to soothe your nerves

02:38.660 --> 02:41.660
and grab the audience's attention
at the same time.

02:41.740 --> 02:42.910
A secret plan?

02:43.000 --> 02:43.910
That's right.

02:45.250 --> 02:46.210
This method…

02:46.290 --> 02:47.750
How is it? It's simple, right?

02:47.830 --> 02:49.420
But it's effective.

02:50.090 --> 02:51.130
Yeah.

02:51.210 --> 02:52.510
I'll give it a try.

02:52.590 --> 02:54.300
Are you rehearsing for tomorrow?

02:55.510 --> 02:57.220
Are you done with your work?

02:57.300 --> 02:58.890
Yes, it went smoothly.

03:00.470 --> 03:02.890
What's wrong, Masachika?

03:02.970 --> 03:05.060
Your expression looks scary.

03:05.140 --> 03:08.310
How can you say that so brazenly?

03:08.400 --> 03:11.820
By the way,
did your ladylike mask come off?

03:11.900 --> 03:13.320
Goodness.

03:14.150 --> 03:15.110
See?

03:15.190 --> 03:18.530
This is her true nature. Don't be fooled.

03:18.620 --> 03:19.700
Okay.

03:19.780 --> 03:21.530
Goodness, Alya.

03:21.620 --> 03:23.580
Are you disillusioned with me?

03:24.330 --> 03:25.410
No.

03:25.500 --> 03:27.290
I'm not disillusioned.

03:28.370 --> 03:29.920
When the situation changes,

03:30.000 --> 03:33.090
one naturally reveals
the unseen side of themselves.

03:33.170 --> 03:34.130
Besides,

03:34.210 --> 03:37.550
you really want
to be friends with me, right?

03:37.630 --> 03:39.970
Yeah, that's true.

03:40.050 --> 03:41.300
Then there's no problem.

03:41.890 --> 03:43.390
After all, thanks to you, Yuki,

03:43.470 --> 03:45.810
I was able to reevaluate myself.

03:45.890 --> 03:47.060
What do you mean?

03:47.140 --> 03:48.600
Back then, you asked me

03:48.690 --> 03:51.690
why I wanted to become
the student council president.

03:51.770 --> 03:53.320
Tomorrow,

03:53.400 --> 03:55.190
I'll show you the answer.

03:57.450 --> 03:59.950
Alya, you really are a straightforward

04:00.030 --> 04:01.700
and wonderful person.

04:03.160 --> 04:04.870
Goodness, this is great.

04:04.950 --> 04:07.460
I'm glad that your friendship
with Alya is intact.

04:07.540 --> 04:10.210
Goodness. When you put it that way,

04:10.290 --> 04:12.630
why does it sound like
my friendship with you

04:12.710 --> 04:15.090
has developed a rift?

04:15.170 --> 04:17.300
No, that's not true.

04:17.380 --> 04:20.840
I'm just wondering
how dare you do such a thing.

04:21.470 --> 04:22.850
Are you angry?

04:22.930 --> 04:25.100
No such thing.

04:25.180 --> 04:27.350
Making a move when the opponents are weak

04:27.430 --> 04:29.850
is a common tactic.

04:30.440 --> 04:31.520
Goodness.

04:31.600 --> 04:33.610
What is this feeling?

04:33.690 --> 04:36.480
I don't really get it though.

04:36.570 --> 04:38.360
But if I had to say,

04:38.440 --> 04:40.320
it's like dealing with a biting dog.

04:40.410 --> 04:43.620
I want to pet it and love it,

04:43.700 --> 04:48.330
but I also want to discipline it
so that it won't bite again.

04:48.960 --> 04:50.420
If it dares to bite,

04:50.500 --> 04:52.130
it'd better grit its teeth.

04:54.500 --> 04:55.880
There you guys are.

04:55.960 --> 04:57.510
Hello.

04:57.590 --> 05:00.090
I want to do
the final confirmation for tomorrow.

05:00.970 --> 05:02.140
First of all,

05:02.220 --> 05:04.180
how do you want to go about

05:04.260 --> 05:05.350
the speech order?

05:05.430 --> 05:08.390
Last year, we had the candidates
decide by rock-paper-scissors.

05:08.470 --> 05:10.640
I don't mind rock-paper-scissors.

05:10.730 --> 05:12.190
No, we can't.

05:12.270 --> 05:14.690
Rock-paper-scissors
is just a game of eyesight.

05:14.770 --> 05:15.610
What?

05:15.690 --> 05:17.230
Well, you're right.

05:17.730 --> 05:20.280
Then why don't we decide by a coin toss?

05:20.360 --> 05:22.280
That would be fairer.

05:22.360 --> 05:23.610
I understand.

05:23.700 --> 05:25.120
Ayano will flip the coin,

05:25.200 --> 05:27.790
and Alya will call heads or tails.

05:27.870 --> 05:30.330
No, someone else will flip the coin.

05:31.250 --> 05:33.040
You're so paranoid.

05:33.120 --> 05:34.500
All right.

05:34.580 --> 05:36.290
Then I'll do it!

05:36.380 --> 05:38.210
Well, Masha, if you're okay with it,

05:38.300 --> 05:39.300
thank you.

05:39.880 --> 05:40.970
If Alya gets it right,

05:41.050 --> 05:42.970
she can choose to go first or second.

05:43.050 --> 05:44.010
If she gets it wrong,

05:44.090 --> 05:45.720
Yuki will get to choose.

05:46.390 --> 05:49.140
Masha, can you really flip it?

05:49.220 --> 05:51.890
What do you take your sister for?

05:51.980 --> 05:53.560
Of course, I can.

05:53.640 --> 05:55.520
Watch me.

06:01.190 --> 06:03.610
<i>If I can go first and look like
I've got it in the bag,</i>

06:03.700 --> 06:05.700
<i>a landslide victory is possible.</i>

06:05.780 --> 06:07.160
<i>But if I go second,</i>

06:07.240 --> 06:10.790
<i>the first person who sets the bar
will still get the minimum applause.</i>

06:10.870 --> 06:14.210
<i>So if I let Alya go first,
a landslide win will be hard.</i>

06:14.290 --> 06:15.960
<i>I guess I should go first, right?</i>

06:16.040 --> 06:20.550
<i>No. I'll go second and see
what my brother does first.</i>

06:21.260 --> 06:22.630
<i>But still…</i>

06:22.720 --> 06:25.470
<i>Why does he have to scare me so blatantly?</i>

06:25.550 --> 06:28.930
<i>It's unlike my cunning brother
to do something like that.</i>

06:30.100 --> 06:30.930
Hi-yah.

06:31.020 --> 06:32.230
I caught it.

06:32.310 --> 06:34.600
Look, I did it, Alya.

06:34.690 --> 06:36.400
Okay, I got it.

06:36.480 --> 06:37.520
Heads it is then.

06:37.610 --> 06:40.190
Hey, give it a little more thought.

06:40.270 --> 06:41.940
That's not necessary.

06:43.070 --> 06:44.530
Well then, I'm opening it.

06:45.030 --> 06:46.660
Goodness, you got it wrong.

06:46.740 --> 06:47.990
Well then, Yuki.

06:48.070 --> 06:50.580
Do you want to go first or second?

06:50.660 --> 06:51.910
Let me think.

06:52.410 --> 06:56.250
<i>Was my brother's attitude just an act?</i>

06:56.330 --> 06:58.040
<i>If so, what's his goal?</i>

06:58.130 --> 07:00.290
<i>Does he want to have
a head-to-head battle with me</i>

07:00.380 --> 07:02.800
<i>to distract me from something?</i>

07:03.460 --> 07:04.720
<i>Alya.</i>

07:05.300 --> 07:06.180
<i>That's right.</i>

07:06.260 --> 07:08.890
<i>Although I was unknowingly
distracted by my brother,</i>

07:08.970 --> 07:11.850
<i>my original target was Alya.</i>

07:11.930 --> 07:15.180
<i>Moreover, Alya's mental state
is more fragile than I thought.</i>

07:15.270 --> 07:18.310
<i>She was also traumatized
by yesterday's school broadcast.</i>

07:18.400 --> 07:19.610
<i>I had anticipated this</i>

07:19.690 --> 07:23.900
<i>and planned to give Alya
the second spot with more pressure.</i>

07:23.990 --> 07:25.400
<i>It seems like his real goal</i>

07:25.490 --> 07:27.820
<i>is to draw the first spot
that gets minimum applause</i>

07:27.910 --> 07:29.370
<i>so that Alya and I can tie.</i>

07:29.450 --> 07:30.280
<i>If so,</i>

07:30.370 --> 07:33.580
<i>I'll just stick to my original plan
and aim for a sweeping victory.</i>

07:34.080 --> 07:37.120
Then, I want to go first.

07:37.210 --> 07:38.540
All right.

07:38.620 --> 07:40.960
Suou and Kimishima will go first.

07:41.040 --> 07:43.750
Kujou and Kuze will go second.

07:43.840 --> 07:45.010
-Yes.
-All right.

07:48.510 --> 07:50.260
CLOSING CEREMONY

07:50.340 --> 07:52.180
Looking back on this semester,

07:52.260 --> 07:55.770
I'm sure you've learned a lot from it.

07:55.850 --> 07:57.060
In the second semester,

07:57.140 --> 07:59.770
we'll continue
to raise awareness of public morals.

08:00.560 --> 08:04.730
Next, we'll hear a few words from
this year's student council executives.

08:05.230 --> 08:08.530
First, we have the student council
president, Touya Kenzaki.

08:12.280 --> 08:13.240
Everyone.

08:13.330 --> 08:15.700
Thank you for your hard work
this semester.

08:15.790 --> 08:19.370
It's been two months
since the new student council took over.

08:19.460 --> 08:21.380
Although we have fewer members this year,

08:21.460 --> 08:23.540
all the executives are outstanding.

08:23.630 --> 08:24.500
Everyone.

08:24.590 --> 08:27.260
Even if it's summer break,
don't slack off too much.

08:27.340 --> 08:28.720
Work hard on your homework

08:28.800 --> 08:30.640
and build your muscles every day.

08:32.260 --> 08:35.470
It's important to train hard every day.

08:35.560 --> 08:39.390
Maybe I'll take a walk
to the park every day too.

08:39.480 --> 08:42.190
Speaking of walks, the other day…

08:43.150 --> 08:46.440
Now, Yuki Suou will give a speech.

08:49.030 --> 08:51.360
Well then, let's go, Ayano.

08:51.450 --> 08:53.070
Yes, Mistress Yuki.

09:01.170 --> 09:03.080
I'm the student council PR officer,

09:03.170 --> 09:06.460
Yuki Suou,
introduced earlier by the emcee.

09:06.550 --> 09:07.880
I'm set to run

09:07.960 --> 09:12.470
for student council president next year.

09:12.550 --> 09:15.220
I look forward to your support.

09:15.300 --> 09:16.390
You can do it!

09:16.470 --> 09:17.970
I'll be rooting for you!

09:18.060 --> 09:19.980
Thank you.

09:20.730 --> 09:22.810
Well then, regarding this matter,

09:22.900 --> 09:26.020
I'd like to share my vision first.

09:26.570 --> 09:29.940
My goal after becoming
the student council president

09:30.030 --> 09:31.240
is to make this place

09:31.320 --> 09:33.740
an academy that reflects
the students' opinions.

09:35.120 --> 09:35.990
Goodness.

09:36.080 --> 09:38.830
Do you think that
it's more ordinary than you imagined?

09:42.040 --> 09:44.960
Specifically, this suggestion box.

09:45.040 --> 09:47.800
It's been in the school
for a few years now

09:47.880 --> 09:52.220
but I don't think many of you
have even used it once.

09:53.300 --> 09:54.800
Actually,

09:54.890 --> 09:57.890
I've been promoting it
through the school broadcast.

09:57.970 --> 10:01.350
But only a handful
have used the suggestion box.

10:02.270 --> 10:03.480
The reason this happens

10:03.560 --> 10:07.190
is because you think
it won't come true even if you write it

10:07.270 --> 10:09.480
and it's just a waste of time, right?

10:09.570 --> 10:10.570
Indeed.

10:10.650 --> 10:11.990
I do think that way.

10:12.070 --> 10:14.910
But I'm not surprised
that you think that way.

10:14.990 --> 10:16.410
Most of the executives

10:16.490 --> 10:19.490
are new to student council work.

10:19.580 --> 10:21.580
They have a lot on their plate.

10:21.660 --> 10:25.500
So it's hard for them to listen
and fulfill your requests.

10:26.540 --> 10:27.750
However,

10:27.840 --> 10:30.380
if I'm elected
as the student council president,

10:30.460 --> 10:32.130
I'll fulfill your suggestions.

10:32.630 --> 10:33.670
To be more specific,

10:33.760 --> 10:35.840
I can help you change
the sports day's events

10:35.930 --> 10:39.510
or expand the content and duration
of the school festival.

10:39.600 --> 10:40.560
In addition,

10:40.640 --> 10:42.310
wouldn't it be fun

10:42.390 --> 10:46.230
to come up with something new
for Halloween or Christmas?

10:49.110 --> 10:52.070
I believe that only someone like me,
who has served

10:52.150 --> 10:54.360
as student council president
in junior high…

10:54.450 --> 10:56.610
And is currently a student council member

10:56.700 --> 11:00.530
with vast achievements and experience,
can accomplish these tasks.

11:01.120 --> 11:03.620
Thank you for listening.

11:05.290 --> 11:07.040
That's not fair.

11:07.120 --> 11:09.750
She's just painting
as rosy a picture as possible

11:09.840 --> 11:12.210
without specifying what she's going to do.

11:12.300 --> 11:14.510
But she's good.

11:14.590 --> 11:16.930
She just might be better than me…

11:17.010 --> 11:19.260
Alya, are you okay?

11:19.350 --> 11:20.760
I'm fine.

11:20.850 --> 11:22.390
Don't worry about me now.

11:22.470 --> 11:24.810
Seriously, at a time like this?

11:26.270 --> 11:27.310
Who is she?

11:27.400 --> 11:29.110
Who knew we had such a beauty on campus!

11:29.650 --> 11:32.570
I'm the general affairs officer,
Ayano Kimishima.

11:32.650 --> 11:35.490
Privately, I'm a servant
of the Suou family.

11:35.570 --> 11:37.570
Currently, I'm Mistress Yuki's retainer.

11:38.160 --> 11:39.120
What does retainer mean?

11:39.200 --> 11:40.070
Beats me.

11:40.660 --> 11:41.990
Also, next year,

11:42.080 --> 11:46.660
I plan to run in the election
with Mistress Yuki.

11:47.290 --> 11:49.290
Mistress Yuki has a good character.

11:49.380 --> 11:52.210
She's an outstanding individual
with both beauty and talent.

11:52.880 --> 11:55.460
However, she never gets complacent.

11:55.550 --> 11:58.300
She's always considerate of others.

12:00.680 --> 12:02.890
What an impeccable speech.

12:02.970 --> 12:07.060
It seems they're going first on purpose,
aiming for a shutout.

12:07.140 --> 12:08.020
Are you okay?

12:08.100 --> 12:08.980
I'm fine.

12:09.060 --> 12:10.350
That's good.

12:10.440 --> 12:13.320
Do you remember the name of this event?

12:13.400 --> 12:15.730
It's speeches by the executives, right?

12:15.820 --> 12:17.780
That's right. It's a speech.

12:17.860 --> 12:20.870
That's why we're going
to let everyone get to know you first.

12:20.950 --> 12:24.030
I have faith that
as the student council president,

12:24.120 --> 12:27.910
she'll be able to lead this academy well.

12:28.000 --> 12:30.880
Thank you for listening.

12:36.960 --> 12:38.470
Well then, our next speaker

12:38.550 --> 12:41.140
is the student council treasurer,
Alisa Kujou.

12:49.310 --> 12:50.810
That girl is pretty interesting.

12:50.900 --> 12:52.310
Kimishima, was it?

12:52.400 --> 12:54.520
Suou's pair is amazing.

12:54.610 --> 12:57.820
She's practically
the next student council president.

13:00.570 --> 13:01.910
You're right.

13:37.480 --> 13:38.480
Excuse me.

13:38.570 --> 13:41.240
I was so nervous that I spoke in Russian.

13:44.740 --> 13:46.030
Was that a joke?

13:46.120 --> 13:47.280
I think so.

13:47.370 --> 13:49.200
No way.

13:50.370 --> 13:51.290
<i>Listen.</i>

13:51.870 --> 13:53.290
If you go second,

13:53.370 --> 13:55.460
you have to start with Russian.

13:55.540 --> 13:59.880
I'm sure Yuki and Ayano will turn
the atmosphere in their favor.

13:59.960 --> 14:02.010
You have to speak in your native language

14:02.090 --> 14:04.180
and throw a wrench in their plan.

14:05.510 --> 14:06.890
Let me introduce myself again.

14:06.970 --> 14:09.560
I'm the student council treasurer,
Alisa Kujou.

14:09.640 --> 14:10.980
I'm set to run

14:11.060 --> 14:14.060
for student council president next year.

14:15.400 --> 14:18.690
I just transferred
to this academy last year.

14:18.770 --> 14:22.070
I have yet to have any achievements
that I can be proud of.

14:22.650 --> 14:24.360
And I can't say for sure

14:24.450 --> 14:26.620
that I fully understand
the duties of an executive

14:26.700 --> 14:29.370
or the heavy responsibilities
of being a president.

14:29.450 --> 14:31.120
In my current state,

14:31.200 --> 14:33.660
I'm sure I have a long way to go
to become the president.

14:34.160 --> 14:36.210
But if there's one thing

14:36.290 --> 14:39.000
that I can be proud of,

14:39.670 --> 14:41.170
it's that…

14:42.260 --> 14:47.010
I can work harder than anyone else.

14:47.090 --> 14:48.800
I've always worked hard

14:48.890 --> 14:51.770
to achieve the results that I want.

14:51.850 --> 14:54.810
I've never become complacent
by relying on my innate talents.

14:54.890 --> 14:56.480
I think continuous self-improvement

14:56.560 --> 14:58.980
is the most important thing as a person.

14:59.060 --> 15:00.070
Indeed.

15:00.150 --> 15:01.610
This extreme way of thinking

15:01.690 --> 15:03.400
<i>sometimes causes friction with others,</i>

15:03.490 --> 15:05.650
<i>and I've even experienced
terrible failures.</i>

15:06.360 --> 15:08.070
But I learn from my failures.

15:08.160 --> 15:09.910
At last year's school festival,

15:09.990 --> 15:12.910
our booth won the Excellence Award.

15:13.750 --> 15:14.790
Of course,

15:14.870 --> 15:17.420
I didn't do it alone.

15:18.000 --> 15:19.920
I know that right now,

15:20.000 --> 15:22.670
I still have a long way to go

15:22.760 --> 15:24.550
before becoming the president.

15:30.470 --> 15:31.930
I know it.

15:32.010 --> 15:33.310
You're more sincere than anyone,

15:33.890 --> 15:36.310
and you'll give your best
no matter what you do.

15:37.060 --> 15:39.100
<i>Look straight ahead, Alya.</i>

15:41.150 --> 15:45.610
But I'm able to speak
in front of everyone like this now

15:45.690 --> 15:46.990
with my own mouth,

15:47.070 --> 15:48.320
with my own words.

15:48.910 --> 15:52.370
And from now on, I'll continue this way

15:52.450 --> 15:54.830
and tackle my shortcomings one by one.

15:55.410 --> 15:57.500
If I can't confirm whether I'm fit

15:57.580 --> 16:01.170
to become the student council president
before next year's election,

16:01.250 --> 16:03.420
I will voluntarily withdraw.

16:04.420 --> 16:05.590
So, everyone,

16:05.670 --> 16:08.090
please keep an eye on me from now on.

16:08.680 --> 16:10.590
I'll use your guidance
as motivation to grow

16:10.680 --> 16:14.850
and become the student council president
that you've all been waiting for.

16:15.640 --> 16:18.600
Thank you for listening.

16:29.200 --> 16:30.280
Good work.

16:30.360 --> 16:32.200
That was really good.

16:32.280 --> 16:33.370
Really?

16:33.450 --> 16:35.620
Yes, you were really cool.

16:37.370 --> 16:39.620
I think I overcame
my mental barrier a little.

16:39.710 --> 16:43.090
Next, Masachika Kuze will give a speech.

16:43.170 --> 16:44.210
Do your best.

16:44.290 --> 16:45.500
Leave it to me.

16:45.590 --> 16:46.880
Well then,

16:46.960 --> 16:48.380
I'll secure our victory in no time.

16:55.560 --> 16:56.520
Hello, everyone.

16:56.600 --> 16:59.180
I'm the general affairs officer,
Masachika Kuze.

16:59.270 --> 17:00.140
Furthermore,

17:00.230 --> 17:04.900
the Vice President in the Shadows
who aided President Yuki Suou

17:04.980 --> 17:06.280
is also me.

17:08.240 --> 17:09.110
That's odd…

17:09.190 --> 17:11.530
Hey, that fell short.

17:16.120 --> 17:17.290
Oh, well.

17:17.370 --> 17:19.790
I'm sure many of you know

17:19.870 --> 17:22.370
that I used to be the vice president.

17:22.460 --> 17:23.630
At this point, I'm sure

17:23.710 --> 17:25.250
you're all wondering,

17:25.340 --> 17:26.250
"What?"

17:26.340 --> 17:29.210
"Then why didn't you run with Suou?"

17:29.300 --> 17:31.970
"Is this an affair?
It's an affair, isn't it?"

17:33.340 --> 17:35.300
I'd like to say one thing.

17:35.390 --> 17:37.600
I already dumped Yuki,

17:37.680 --> 17:40.020
so it's not an affair!

17:40.100 --> 17:41.390
You're the worst!

17:41.480 --> 17:43.440
You moved on too quickly.

17:46.650 --> 17:48.820
Then, why did I dump Yuki

17:48.900 --> 17:51.280
and support Alya instead?

17:51.360 --> 17:52.280
Everyone,

17:52.360 --> 17:56.160
what kind of person do you think
should be the student council president?

17:56.240 --> 17:58.910
Is it someone who's good
at their job and responsible?

17:58.990 --> 18:00.830
Or someone who's mentally strong?

18:01.910 --> 18:03.620
I think neither.

18:04.790 --> 18:07.380
The one suited to be the president

18:07.460 --> 18:10.340
should be someone who can attract people.

18:11.670 --> 18:12.800
Everyone,

18:12.880 --> 18:14.890
when you heard Alya's speech just then,

18:14.970 --> 18:16.220
what did you think?

18:16.850 --> 18:19.560
I thought she was really clumsy.

18:20.060 --> 18:21.600
But at the same time,

18:21.680 --> 18:25.100
I felt like her speech
was very sincere and honest.

18:25.850 --> 18:27.980
Alya is an honest person.

18:28.070 --> 18:30.360
Even when I suggested
giving the speech in Russian,

18:30.440 --> 18:32.240
she just accepted it.

18:33.200 --> 18:34.820
The reason I didn't support Yuki

18:34.910 --> 18:36.740
and supported Alya instead

18:36.820 --> 18:38.740
is because I was drawn
to this trait of hers.

18:38.830 --> 18:40.240
That's why I want to root for her.

18:40.910 --> 18:42.290
And I hope all of you

18:42.370 --> 18:44.960
can also root for Alya.

18:46.460 --> 18:47.880
Even so,

18:47.960 --> 18:49.210
I think my opinion alone

18:49.290 --> 18:51.170
isn't that credible, right?

18:51.260 --> 18:53.880
Therefore, I have something
to share with you.

18:54.760 --> 18:57.640
If Alya gets elected
as the student council president,

18:57.720 --> 18:59.890
Sayaka Taniyama and Nonoa Miyamae

18:59.970 --> 19:02.180
will join our team
as student council executives.

19:02.270 --> 19:03.140
What?

19:04.850 --> 19:07.060
Can you believe it?

19:07.150 --> 19:09.400
Our previous rivals in the general meeting

19:09.480 --> 19:13.030
are willing to work together
in the new student council.

19:15.240 --> 19:16.530
What? No way.

19:16.610 --> 19:17.660
Hey, look over there.

19:17.740 --> 19:19.450
Seriously?

19:25.750 --> 19:28.080
That concludes my speech.

19:28.170 --> 19:31.460
In order to create
an unprecedented student council,

19:31.550 --> 19:34.170
I sincerely ask for your support.

19:41.430 --> 19:42.760
Alya.

19:42.850 --> 19:45.180
You earned this applause with your power.

19:54.570 --> 19:56.490
We're even now.

19:56.570 --> 19:58.200
Yes, thank you.

19:58.280 --> 19:59.700
You're a lifesaver.

19:59.780 --> 20:02.530
This is the only time
I'll help you in this election.

20:02.620 --> 20:03.830
I know.

20:03.910 --> 20:06.500
In order to get your support,

20:06.580 --> 20:07.710
I'll work hard.

20:08.920 --> 20:10.290
I look forward to it.

20:10.790 --> 20:12.920
Well then, do your best.

20:13.000 --> 20:15.340
If Alisha becomes
the student council president,

20:15.420 --> 20:17.170
I'll come and help.

20:18.050 --> 20:20.220
Alisha?

20:23.810 --> 20:27.430
<i>This is the reason why I'm running
for student council president.</i>

20:27.520 --> 20:30.190
<i>From now on,
I will never give in to your resolve.</i>

20:31.860 --> 20:33.690
They got us.

20:34.190 --> 20:35.860
I'm very sorry.

20:35.940 --> 20:39.200
If only I could have said it better.

20:39.280 --> 20:41.620
It's not your fault, Ayano.

20:41.700 --> 20:43.330
I was too calculating.

20:43.410 --> 20:45.080
That's why I misjudged.

20:45.700 --> 20:46.750
Anyway,

20:46.830 --> 20:49.250
I'll admit defeat this time.

20:49.330 --> 20:51.670
But only this time.

20:52.170 --> 20:53.540
Mistress Yuki.

20:54.040 --> 20:56.210
This strong aura of yours is awesome.

20:57.920 --> 20:59.880
No, I didn't mean to create that vibe.

21:05.310 --> 21:10.190
It would be even cooler
if I could achieve this goal too.

21:10.690 --> 21:12.350
That's right.

21:12.440 --> 21:14.980
What a disappointing result.

21:15.070 --> 21:16.980
I guess even a genius like me

21:17.070 --> 21:18.900
has his limits.

21:18.990 --> 21:20.360
Do you hear yourself?

21:20.450 --> 21:22.450
So, do you regret the result?

21:22.530 --> 21:23.450
No!

21:23.530 --> 21:26.080
That's good. Let's go home then.

21:26.160 --> 21:27.580
A lot has happened today.

21:27.660 --> 21:29.330
I'm a bit tired.

21:29.410 --> 21:31.160
Yes, you're right.

21:33.670 --> 21:34.880
Hey, Alya.

21:34.960 --> 21:35.840
What's the matter?

21:35.920 --> 21:37.460
No, well,

21:37.550 --> 21:39.170
what about the bet?

21:39.260 --> 21:42.090
Didn't you say I'd owe you a wish
if I don't achieve it?

21:42.720 --> 21:44.340
I'll think about it seriously.

21:44.430 --> 21:45.390
Hold on.

21:45.470 --> 21:47.930
Didn't you say you've thought about it?

21:48.020 --> 21:49.930
And you said something in Russian?

21:50.020 --> 21:51.060
Well,

21:51.140 --> 21:53.690
it was just a casual remark.

21:54.940 --> 21:56.400
What?

21:56.480 --> 21:58.690
I thought for sure that you'd…

21:59.690 --> 22:01.490
<i>I see,</i>

22:01.570 --> 22:04.660
<i>she never thought that she'd win?</i>

22:04.740 --> 22:06.780
<i>Let's see, what was it again?</i>

22:06.870 --> 22:08.950
<i>I think it was about my name.</i>

22:11.040 --> 22:12.870
Alya.

22:13.750 --> 22:17.420
Well, we've already given our speeches
before the whole school

22:17.500 --> 22:21.510
and have been officially recognized
as a pair in the presidential election.

22:21.590 --> 22:22.590
At this time,

22:22.670 --> 22:25.590
to show how close we are,

22:25.680 --> 22:29.010
why don't we call each other
by our first names?

22:29.930 --> 22:32.270
Well, that's a good idea.

22:32.350 --> 22:33.600
What? Is that so?

22:33.690 --> 22:34.980
I… I guess so.

22:37.190 --> 22:39.690
Well, then…

22:41.280 --> 22:43.110
Masa… chika.

22:45.450 --> 22:48.080
S-Sure, I'm okay with that…

22:48.160 --> 22:49.580
Is… is that so?

22:49.660 --> 22:51.120
Well then, from now on,

22:51.200 --> 22:52.410
I'll call you that.

22:52.500 --> 22:53.410
Okay.

22:54.250 --> 22:55.710
Right!

22:55.790 --> 22:57.130
We have to change our shoes.

22:57.210 --> 22:58.500
You're right.

23:06.130 --> 23:07.010
Alya.

23:08.010 --> 23:11.390
Well, summer break is coming up,

23:11.470 --> 23:14.560
but we still have to prepare
for the election, right?

23:14.640 --> 23:17.940
I'm sure Yuki and Ayano
will be together all the time.

23:18.520 --> 23:20.230
So…

23:21.110 --> 23:25.200
during summer break,
why don't we see each other often too?

23:30.240 --> 23:31.700
Masachika.

23:33.250 --> 23:35.000
Look ahead.

23:38.960 --> 23:40.210
Gladly.
